ilestones/57/labels","id":1267159,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lMTI2NzE1OQ==","number":57,"title":"3.0.13","description":"Bugfixes and minor enhancements for 3.0.x","creator":{"login":"markstory","id":24086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory","html_url":"https://github.com/markstory","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":48,"state":"closed","created_at":"2015-08-22T01:47:51Z","updated_at":"2015-09-07T02:11:22Z","due_on":"2015-09-06T04:00:00Z","closed_at":"2015-09-07T02:11:22Z"},"comments":15,"created_at":"2015-07-31T07:45:34Z","updated_at":"2015-08-24T06:22:58Z","closed_at":"2015-08-24T06:22:58Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"After using the 'matching' method in a subquery the paginator component throws an error: SQLSTATE[HY093]: Invalid parameter number: number of bound variables does not match number of tokens\nThis happens when the paginatorcomponent tries to count the total results. \n- Subscription belongsToMany Statuses\n- Subscription belongsTo Routes\n- Routes belongsTo RouteDepartures && RouteDestionations\n\nIn controller: \n\n```\n        $filter = array_filter([\n            'route_departure_id' => $this->request->query('route_departure_id'),\n            'route_destination_id' => $this->request->query('route_destination_id')\n        ]);\n\n        $this->paginate = [\n            'finder' => [\n                'report' => ['filter' => $filter]\n            ]\n        ];\n\n        $report = $this->paginate();\n```\n\nCustom finder (in RoutesTable):\n\n```\n    public function findReport($query, array $options = [])\n    {\n        $subscriptions = $this->Subscriptions->find();\n        $subscriptions\n            ->select([\n                $subscriptions->func()->count('Subscriptions.id')\n            ])\n            ->where(['route_id = Routes.id'])\n            ->matching('Statuses', function ($q) {\n                return $q->where(['Statuses.code' => 302]);\n            });\n\n        return $query\n            ->select([\n                'RouteDepartures.name',\n                'RouteDestinations.name',\n                'subscriptions' => $subscriptions\n            ])\n            ->contain([\n                'RouteDepartures',\n                'RouteDestinations'\n            ])\n            ->where($options['filter']);\n    }\n```\n\nAs long as I don't use the filter, the paginator works like it should. But as soon as I use the where condition it falls flat on its face. \nIs there a problem in my custom finder?\nIt seems to me that the number of parameters is not reset before calling count() in paginator component. The query that throws the error has the original two parameters from the custom finder, but uses only one (and thus trhows an error):\n\n```\nSELECT (COUNT(*)) AS `count` FROM routes Routes INNER JOIN route_departures RouteDepartures ON RouteDepartures.id = (Routes.route_departure_id) INNER JOIN route_destinations RouteDestinations ON RouteDestinations.id = (Routes.route_destination_id) WHERE (route_destination_id = :c0 AND Routes.deleted IS NULL)\n```\n\nI'll try to create a failing test, but I'm not yet sure if the problem is mine or in Cakephp...\n","closed_by":{"login":"jc-vogel","id":12329293,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzI5Mjkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12329293?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel","html_url":"https://github.com/jc-vogel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc-vogel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/7148/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/7148/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}